{
  "name": "create-variable-and-its-accesses",
  "description": "An inter-runnable variable and a runnable's two accesses to it, authored with no new tool and no new addressing (contract `12.1.0`): the variable is a `create` at its `field`-identified member address under the component's `variables`, `{member: <name>}`, and each access a `create` at its own member address under the runnable's `reads_variables` or `writes_variables`, identified by the `variable` it names. The runnable exists already, so the delta reports each of the three creates as its own reviewed entry.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The `examples/basic` model. `ExampleSWC` declares no variable, and its one runnable, `ExampleRun`, accesses none. The variable is implementation-typed by the base's `uint8` and carries an `init`, so `check-model`'s read-without-init warning has nothing to say, and the safety rules read no variable, so the change set asks no safety question. One runnable reading and writing one variable is a shape SWCraft does not judge: no order of execution is modelled.",
    "existing_elements": [
      {
        "layer": "swc",
        "element": "ExampleSWC",
        "path": [
          {
            "field": "runnables"
          },
          {
            "member": "ExampleRun"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "baseline_state": "current",
    "authorization": {
